# Application Consumption

The application should consume the shared library.

```
Application Repository

Taskfile.yml

↓

includes

↓

Platform Task Library
```

Example

```yaml
version: '3'

includes:
  platform:
    taskfile: .platform/taskfile.yml
```

The `.platform` folder is populated automatically during pipeline execution or bootstrap from the approved version of the shared Taskfile Library.

Application developers should never manually copy shared tasks.

---

# Version Support Policy

Not every version should remain supported forever.

Recommended policy:

| Version     | Status     |
| ----------- | ---------- |
| Latest      | Supported  |
| N-1         | Supported  |
| Older       | Deprecated |
| End of Life | Blocked    |

Example

| Platform | Repository | Result    |
| -------- | ---------- | --------- |
| v1.5     | v1.5       | ✅         |
| v1.5     | v1.4       | ✅         |
| v1.5     | v1.2       | ⚠ Warning |
| v1.5     | v1.0       | ❌ Fail    |

---

# CI Validation

Every pipeline should validate the platform version before execution.

```
Pipeline

↓

Read Platform Version

↓

Compare Supported Versions

↓

Pass / Fail
```

This prevents long-term drift across repositories.

---

# Release Process

```
Platform Team

↓

Development

↓

Testing

↓

Release v1.5

↓

Pilot Applications

↓

Organization Rollout

↓

Deprecate Older Versions
```

Every release should include:

* Release notes
* Breaking changes
* Upgrade guide
* Migration examples

---

# Exception Process

Sometimes immediate upgrades aren't possible.

Example

| Repository | Current Version | Approved Until |
| ---------- | --------------- | -------------- |
| Claims API | v1.2            | 31-Dec-2026    |

After the expiry date, pipelines fail unless renewed.

---

# Version Dashboard

Platform Engineering should maintain visibility.

Example

| Repository | Platform Version | Status            |
| ---------- | ---------------- | ----------------- |
| Claims API | v1.5             | Current           |
| Billing    | v1.4             | Upgrade Available |
| Policy     | v1.2             | Unsupported       |

